                           </imprint>
                           <title level="a" xml:id="title_2bbfbb24">Kirkekoncert</title>
                           <title level="j" xml:id="title_03a24009">Dagbladet</title>
                           <biblScope unit="issue" xml:id="biblScope_2ccb16bd">95</biblScope>
                           <biblScope unit="page" xml:id="biblScope_e5a3e921">2</biblScope>
                        </bibl>
                     </biblList>
                     <biblList xml:id="biblList_1602784c">
                        <head xml:id="head_8eaeb4b8">Evidence</head>
                     </biblList>
                  </event>
               </eventList>
               <p xml:id="idm138">Adolf Langsted at the request of Hartmann in December 1887, sent him some information concerning those songs in his "Et Korstog. En religiøs-romantisk Digtning" (A Crusade. A Religious-Romantic Poem) which were suited for music. He especially recommended "Martyrhymne", which he characterized as "the most important and because of its unusual rhythm most distinctly song". It was Langsted's wish that the songs should be ready in March, but Hartmann did not compose them until the summer of 1888.</p>
            </history>
